  data: {
    LLM: "1. Betting: Every tile in hand has a 'price'. Players pay for hits based on the current number of tiles they hold.\n2. Hitting: Players choose to 'Stand' or 'Hit' (draw a tile). Every time a player takes a hit, they must expose one of their face-down tiles to the table, ensuring they always have two face-down tiles.\n3. Banker's Turn: The banker plays last and chooses when to stand or hit.\n4. Bust: If pips exceed 21, the player loses immediately.",
    Player: "1. Betting: Every tile in hand has a 'price'. Players pay for hits based on the current number of tiles they hold.\n2. Hitting: Players choose to 'Stand' or 'Hit' (draw a tile). Every time a player takes a hit, they must expose one of their face-down tiles to the table, ensuring they always have two face-down tiles.\n3. Banker's Turn: The banker plays last and chooses when to stand or hit.\n4. Bust: If pips exceed 21, the player loses immediately.",
    objective: 'Achieve a total pip count closer to 21 than the banker, without exceeding 21.',
    gameplay: "1. Betting: Every tile in hand has a 'price'. Players pay for hits based on the current number of tiles they hold.\n2. Hitting: Players choose to 'Stand' or 'Hit' (draw a tile). Every time a player takes a hit, they must expose one of their face-down tiles to the table, ensuring they always have two face-down tiles.\n3. Banker's Turn: The banker plays last and chooses when to stand or hit.\n4. Bust: If pips exceed 21, the player loses immediately.",
    keyRules: [
      'The banker wins all ties.',
      'A hand of 9 tiles is the maximum possible hand that can stay under 21.',
      'Payouts are often scaled by the number of tiles held (e.g., winning with 5 tiles pays more than with 2).',
